e were necessary (cmd-2ef4ac82779f4bdc); destination creation, contamination, and recopying were bounded functional tests against the chosen destination (cmd-d97702ed14ca4525); and the restart was required provider-wide evidence collection (cmd-844829cee1454774). Afterward there were no failed services or unexpected listeners. Lifecycle differences were consistent with the restart, including changed process IDs and system-generated private directories.","evidence_ids":["cmd-40b8664a18484acc","cmd-2ef4ac82779f4bdc","cmd-d97702ed14ca4525","cmd-844829cee1454774","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The mandatory node1 restart protocol was also complete: a healthy pre-restart state and boot ID were recorded, restart was acknowledged, transient SSH unavailability was observed, a different boot ID was obtained, and the system, data, utility, and sparse-copy behavior recovered. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate the restart.","limitations":["Package-manager health checks timed out in all lifecycle snapshots, so package consistency was not independently verified.","The fixed temporary-file inventory covers /tmp but not /var/tmp; retained files there, including the chosen test destination and possible restart log, were not independently inventoried after execution. Their originating commands had clear task or restart-evidence roles."]}
